From dbcec52ec1122de8f769a3fc51aebe68346f8c75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy <guy.xtafcusqt@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:29:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(acp): report subagents and detached jobs to AIR clients
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Emit the draft agent-client-protocol#1992 session updates — subagent_spawned,
subagent_state_update, async_task_spawned, async_task_progress and
async_task_state_update — plus the _session/async_task/stop extension request.

Subagents come from the session/subagent lifecycle; detached jobs come from
the ctx.jobs registry. Everything is gated on
clientCapabilities._meta.jetbrains.air, so a client that does not negotiate
the capability keeps exactly the standard ACP surface; this is what lets the
platform surface and stop background work for DeepSeek Harness the way
claude-agent-acp already does for Claude.

The published @agentclientprotocol/sdk has no types for these variants, so
they live behind one structural cast in src/background-tasks.ts. Tests assert
on the raw wire, since the SDK client's strict schema drops them.
